  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "PROPOSED ALTERATION AND ADDITION TO THE EXISTING REAR  EXTENSION, A SINGLE STOREY SIDE EXTENSION, FRONT  GARRAGE EXTENSION, AND CONVERSION  OF GARAGE TO HABITABLE ROOM INCLUDING PORCH",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The proposed single storey rear extension by reason of its depth and height on the boundary with No.8 Home Mead would result in an overbearing structure leading to loss of light,&amp;nbsp; overshadowing and a detrimental sense of enclosure on neighbouring occupiers.&amp;nbsp; As such, the development is contrary Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and guidance in the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm&quot;&gt;The proposed front extension by\r\nreason of its two front doors and porch roof in combination with the front\r\nextension&#x27;s roof would result in incongruous and awkward&amp;nbsp;addition to the\r\ndwellinghouse and street scene contrary to the high quality design aspirations\r\nof the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), D3 D(7) and D(11) of\r\nThe&amp;nbsp; London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy\r\n(2012), Policy DM1(c) of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan\r\n(2013) and guidance in the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential\r\nDesign Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
